---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url";
---

<Base
  title="SciencesLoop — Evidence-gated scientific workflows"
  description="SciencesLoop builds evidence-gated scientific workflow software for brownfield laboratories, starting with electrochemistry."
  alternatePath={u("/zh/")}
>
  <div class="sl-page sl-home">
    <section class="sl-hero">
      <div class="sl-kicker"><span class="sl-signal"></span>Scientific workflow software · in development</div>
      <h1>Evidence before autonomy.</h1>
      <p class="sl-lead">SciencesLoop builds evidence-gated scientific workflow software for brownfield laboratories, starting with electrochemistry.</p>
      <p class="sl-sublead">The first wedge is offline CV/EIS inference and anomaly review: preserve the instrument, add a traceable decision layer, and require human approval when evidence is incomplete.</p>
      <div class="sl-actions">
        <a class="sl-button primary" href={u("/evidence/")}>Inspect current evidence</a>
        <a class="sl-button" href={u("/approach/")}>See the approach</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sl-section">
      <div class="sl-section-head">
        <span>01 · The problem</span>
        <h2>Laboratory decisions still lose their reasoning.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="sl-grid three">
        <article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip risk">Observed gap</span><h3>Fragmented context</h3><p>Instrument files, notebooks, scripts, and expert judgment sit in separate systems.</p></article>
        <article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip risk">Observed gap</span><h3>Weak decision traces</h3><p>A result may be saved without the assumptions, uncertainty, or approval that made it actionable.</p></article>
        <article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip risk">Observed gap</span><h3>Brownfield reality</h3><p>Most laboratories need software that can sit beside existing instruments, not require a clean-room rebuild.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-dark">
      <div class="sl-section-head"><span>02 · The loop</span><h2>A bounded path from claim to decision.</h2></div>
      <div class="sl-trace" aria-label="Claim to decision trace">
        <div><b>01</b><strong>Claim</strong><small>What the workflow is trying to establish</small></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><b>02</b><strong>Evidence</strong><small>Source, provenance, quality, and uncertainty</small></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><b>03</b><strong>Gate</strong><small>Pass, abstain, or request human review</small></div>
        <i aria-hidden="true">→</i>
        <div><b>04</b><strong>Decision</strong><small>A replayable output with explicit limits</small></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sl-section">
      <div class="sl-section-head"><span>03 · Current position</span><h2>Small, inspectable, and honest about the boundary.</h2></div>
      <div class="sl-grid two">
        <article class="sl-card featured"><span class="sl-chip live">Live demonstration</span><h3>Public evidence workflows</h3><p>Runnable demos show bounded identity checks, deterministic analysis, evidence gaps, and human confirmation.</p><p class="sl-limit"><b>They demonstrate:</b> traceable workflow behavior. <b>They do not prove:</b> wet-lab validation or autonomous instrument control.</p><a class="sl-text-link" href={u("/evidence/")}>Review the evidence register →</a></article>
        <article class="sl-card"><span class="sl-chip proposed">Proposed</span><h3>Electrochemistry workflow layer</h3><p>A future product direction for offline CV/EIS inference, anomaly detection, provenance, and approval gates around existing laboratory systems.</p><p class="sl-limit">No production deployment, wet-lab validation, or committed laboratory partnership is claimed.</p><a class="sl-text-link" href={u("/applications/")}>Explore the application wedge →</a></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sl-section sl-contact">
      <div><span class="sl-chip working">Working prototype</span><h2>Build the evidence layer first.</h2><p>SciencesLoop is looking for technically rigorous conversations about scientific workflow reliability and electrochemistry validation.</p></div>
      <a class="sl-button primary" href="mailto:luzhang@sciencesloop.com">Contact SciencesLoop</a>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
